-- title:
--   A five-dimensional space of rational functions of u containing 1, u, u⁻¹ carries a 2×3 configuration iff it is D1, D2a or D2b
-- statement:
--   Let $u \in \mathbb{C}$ be transcendental, that is, $u \notin \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ (the algebraic numbers); spans and linear independence are over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$. Let $W \subseteq \mathbb{C}$ be a $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-vector subspace of dimension $5$ with $1, u, u^{-1} \in W$, that is, $H_0 \subseteq W$ for $H_0 = \mathrm{span}(1, u, u^{-1})$. Suppose every element of $W$ lies in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}(u)$, the subfield of $\mathbb{C}$ generated by $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ and $u$. Then $W$ carries a $2 \times 3$ configuration (linearly independent $x_0, x_1 \in \mathbb{C}$ and linearly independent $y_0, y_1, y_2 \in \mathbb{C}$ with every $x_iy_j \in W$) if and only if one of the following holds:
--
--   - **(D1)** there are linearly independent $t_0, t_1, t_2 \in \mathbb{C}$ with $t_j \in W$ and $ut_j \in W$ for every $j$;
--   - **(D2a, two-orbit)** $W = \mathrm{span}(1, u, u^{-1}, Q'(u)S_1(u)/(uP'(u)), P'(u)S_2(u)/(uQ'(u)))$ for some $P', Q', S_1, S_2 \in \overline{\mathbb{Q}}[X]$ with $P', Q'$ coprime, $\max(\deg P', \deg Q') = 2$ and $\deg S_1, \deg S_2 \leq 2$;
--   - **(D2b, cyclic)** $W = \mathrm{span}(1, u, u^{-1}, Q'(u)S_1(u)/(uP'(u)), Q'(u)(Q'(u)S_1(u) + P'(u)S_2(u))/(uP'(u)^2))$ for some such $P', Q', S_1, S_2$.
--
--   **Proof.** ($\Rightarrow$) `DiazModulus.rational_space_configuration_coprime_ratio` writes $x_1q(u) = x_0p(u)$ with $p, q$ coprime and $\max(\deg p, \deg q) \geq 1$, and `DiazModulus.two_by_three_configuration_ratio_degree_le_two` bounds that degree by $2$. Degree $1$: `DiazModulus.mobius_ratio_configuration_u_multiplier_triple` gives (D1). Degree $2$: Theorem NF (`DiazModulus.degree_two_configuration_normal_form`) gives (D1), (D2a) or (D2b). ($\Leftarrow$) Under (D1), $(1, u) \otimes t$ is a configuration, $1, u$ being independent as $u \notin \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$. Under (D2a) or (D2b), $W$ is the canonical span, of dimension $5$, and `DiazModulus.quadratic_two_orbit_space_carries_two_by_three_configuration`, resp. `DiazModulus.quadratic_cyclic_space_carries_two_by_three_configuration`, give the configuration $(1, P'(u)/Q'(u)) \otimes y$.
--
--   **Novelty.** Not found in the sources read: the “only if” half, the classification. The configurations themselves (the “if” half) give, at a candidate, exclusions that are substitutions in Roy's strong six exponentials theorem (Roy 1992, Cor. 2). Applied to the conjugation hulls of rational $z$, it gives the five-dimensional case of Theorem F (`DiazModulus.rational_conj_hull_two_by_three_configuration_iff`). Theorem F asks the question of Theorem E of the mission's research note (the Laurent case, formal as `DiazModulus.laurent_conj_hull_two_by_three_configuration_iff`) for every $z$ rational in $u$, and builds on Theorem B (`DiazModulus.circle_point_extension_two_by_three_configuration_iff`, 10.6), which holds for every complex $z$. For Laurent $z$, that its answer gives back Theorem E's classes (P), (Q) and (R) was checked by exact computation on random data, not proved; Theorem E's explicit criteria do not follow from it.
-- source:
--   Not found in the sources read: the “only if” half, the classification. Applied to conjugation hulls (with DiazModulus.rational_conj_hull_le_adjoin) it gives the five-dimensional case of Theorem F (DiazModulus.rational_conj_hull_two_by_three_configuration_iff). Theorem F asks the question of Theorem E of the mission's research note on polynomial and Laurent hulls (DiazModulus.laurent_conj_hull_two_by_three_configuration_iff, Laurent z) for every z rational in u, and builds on Theorem B (DiazModulus.circle_point_extension_two_by_three_configuration_iff, 10.6), which holds for every complex z. For Laurent z, agreement with Theorem E's classes was checked by exact computation, not proved. Its configurations give, at a candidate, exclusions that are substitutions in Roy's strong six exponentials theorem (D. Roy, Matrices whose coefficients are linear forms in logarithms, J. Number Theory 41 (1992), 22–47, Cor. 2). Uses DiazModulus.degree_two_configuration_normal_form, DiazModulus.quadratic_two_orbit_space_carries_two_by_three_configuration, DiazModulus.quadratic_cyclic_space_carries_two_by_three_configuration, DiazModulus.rational_space_configuration_coprime_ratio, DiazModulus.mobius_ratio_configuration_u_multiplier_triple and DiazModulus.two_by_three_configuration_ratio_degree_le_two. R20 of the Diaz modulus mission. Formal proof: Diaz modulus mission, 23 October 2026 (C. Perassi).

import Definitions.Def_DiazModulus

open Complex ComplexConjugate

namespace DiazModulus

open Polynomial in
theorem rational_space_two_by_three_configuration_iff (u : ℂ) (hu : u ∉ Qbar) (W : Submodule (↥Qbar) ℂ) [FiniteDimensional (↥Qbar) W]
    (hW : Module.finrank (↥Qbar) W = 5) (h1 : (1 : ℂ) ∈ W) (hu1 : u ∈ W) (hui : u⁻¹ ∈ W)
    (hrat : ∀ w ∈ W, w ∈ IntermediateField.adjoin Qbar ({u} : Set ℂ)) :
    (∃ (x : Fin 2 → ℂ) (y : Fin 3 → ℂ), LinearIndependent (↥Qbar) x ∧ LinearIndependent (↥Qbar) y ∧
        ∀ i j, x i * y j ∈ W) ↔
    (∃ t : Fin 3 → ℂ, LinearIndependent (↥Qbar) t ∧ ∀ j, t j ∈ W ∧ u * t j ∈ W) ∨ (∃ P' Q' S₁ S₂ : (↥Qbar)[X], IsCoprime P' Q' ∧ max P'.natDegree Q'.natDegree = 2 ∧
        S₁.natDegree ≤ 2 ∧ S₂.natDegree ≤ 2 ∧
        W = Submodule.span Qbar ({1, u, u⁻¹, aeval u Q' * aeval u S₁ / (u * aeval u P'),
          aeval u P' * aeval u S₂ / (u * aeval u Q')} : Set ℂ)) ∨
    (∃ P' Q' S₁ S₂ : (↥Qbar)[X], IsCoprime P' Q' ∧ max P'.natDegree Q'.natDegree = 2 ∧
        S₁.natDegree ≤ 2 ∧ S₂.natDegree ≤ 2 ∧
        W = Submodule.span Qbar ({1, u, u⁻¹, aeval u Q' * aeval u S₁ / (u * aeval u P'),
          aeval u Q' * (aeval u Q' * aeval u S₁ + aeval u P' * aeval u S₂) / (u * aeval u P' ^ 2)} :
            Set ℂ)) := by
  sorry

end DiazModulus
